rst_screen.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_presentation_one_reading.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_rung_one_triage.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_scorecard_baseline.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "The different-baselines branch of the change matrix has no test: the control's fallback to its trials passed and each candidate's 'from <control>'s X%' mark are never asserted, and the L3 test exempts such cells instead of closing them", "recommendation": "instance. Where candidates' baselines differ, scorecard.py:549 (held has more than one entry) prints the control's pooled trials count, and scorecard.py:568 adds 'from <control>'s X%' to each cell whose baseline is not the printed level. That branch is the only thing keeping the owner's arithmetic true when candidates ran different case sets. No test builds such a page: test_scorecard_baseline.py:165-166 skips the arithmetic check for any cell holding 'from ' rather than checking it against the stated figure. No page in _CHANGE_PAGES is shown to reach the branch, and no assertion reads the mark's text. Add a shape with two candidates on uneven case sets. Assert three things: the control cell reads its trials passed ('N of M trials'); each candidate's cell names its own baseline; and the candidate's level less that stated baseline equals its change within 0.1. Change line 166 to close against the stated baseline, not skip it.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/campaign/scorecard.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_scorecard_baseline.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The module docstring still says a first-screen rate is never a bare percent, but a candidate's level (23.0%) now prints with no count", "recommendation": "ACCEPT the cell form: plan 4.2 sets '{level} \u00b7 {signed change} pts' with the count only on the control, and the candidate's count is one step down in the fold's 'Arm passed'. The prose at scorecard.py:21-22 now overclaims, so delete the 'never a bare percent' clause or make it relational (a level's count is in the fold). Batch into the fix commit.", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The 'All aspects' row's candidate cells print a signed change with no level, unlike every other candidate cell", "recommendation": "scorecard.py:342 signs the equal-weight change but gives it no `level`, so the row reads '46.7% | +1.7 pts' while plan 4.2 says a candidate cell reads its level then its change. The control's level is in the same row, so the baseline is visible and the owner's bar holds. ACCEPT, or set `level` from the equal-weight control level plus the change. The L3 test skips this row.", "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Plan 4.2's proof for the turned one-arm matrix, 'at 688 px the table fits with no scroll', is not asserted", "recommendation": "test_scorecard_baseline asserts the turned columns and no glyph. test_presentation_host_fit allows a table to scroll if it says so. State it as descoped in the change record, or add a 688 px width assertion for the s3 page in the existing browser file.", "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "A one-arm page's 'measures' fold repeats the turned scorecard row for row where no measure is split by setup", "recommendation": "Duplication, not a defect: the fold adds only the per-setup rows. ACCEPT for now. A later chunk could fold only when `by_rig` holds, or note that the matrix is the whole table.", "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "The candidate head drops 'change' from the plan's 'pass rate, change vs {control}'", "recommendation": "Correct call: 'pass rate, change vs v1' is four words, past style.MAX_HEADER_WORDS = 3. 'v2 \u00b7 pass rate vs v1' names both the measure and the control (L1), the cell's signed '+2.5 pts' and the glyph line's 'change from v1 (the tick)' say it is a change, and the choice is in the docstring at scorecard.py:429-431. ACCEPT; record it in the builder's decisions.", "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "lint_page now excludes arm names inside a header from the three-word cap: a correct fix, not a loosening", "recommendation": "The rule (style.lint_prose) counts a header's own words. Names were already exempt as whole headers (style_support.py:78), and a host's arm name is data, as a quoted question is. Without this, a two-word arm name would break the cap on any head that names it. The header's own words, 'pass rate vs', still sit at the cap. ACCEPT.", "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Three test updates checked: none weakens a contract", "recommendation": "(a) test_presentation_figure_forms.py:199 still walks every scale line. Only the requirement that rung 2 draws money glyphs is dropped, a consequence of plan 4.2's turned one-arm matrix, and the money interval's form there is now held by test_campaign_scorecard's turned-matrix assertions. (b) test_depth_surfaces.py:251-254 is reversed by plan 4.2's 'Precision moves under Methods, folded', and it now asserts more: section, details and the between column. (c) Stripping tags before counting REPEATS_FLOOR can only raise the count, so '== 1' stays at least as strict. It is needed because the line now carries the term's first-use link. ACCEPT all three.", "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "The prose-canary waiver's claim holds", "recommendation": "In src, DisclosureBlock.emphasis is set only at build.py:672 and campaign/page.py:287, both code's verdict decisions run through code_emphasis. The analyst's and chart_query's `emphasis` fields belong to different models (a chart's stressed mark), and no writer path builds a DisclosureBlock. A host constructing one is the only other source. This matches the existing waiver at model.py:130. ACCEPT.", "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Arithmetic, sign, direction, escaping, underscores and the API surface checked", "recommendation": "none. The printed level is round(baseline + change, 1) beside round(baseline, 1) and round(change, 1), so it closes to within 0.1. Spot checks pass: rung 3 81.1 + 16.7 = 97.8, and the reading-reports.md examples close. The change matrix and its fold read only the pass rate, where higher is better, so the hard-coded 'right is better' and the reading words are right. No lower-is-better measure reaches a signed cell or glyph_key. Host text (arm and control labels in heads, flags and glyph_key) goes through code_html or _cell_code, never into an attribute. No new cross-module underscore binding. `TableCell`, `TableBlock` and `DisclosureBlock` snapshot with empty signatures, so api/surface.json needs no regeneration. reference.md gains glyph_key, the one documented model touched. MIGRATIONS names level, signed, glyph_key and code_emphasis. `TableCell.figure`, the new public property html_parts reads, is not named there. That is NOTE-level.", "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "An exact zero change reads '0 pts' beside '-5.0 pts' in one column, and the turned matrix's interval can differ in precision from its value", "recommendation": "Both are plan 4.5's one-precision-per-set rule (O5), which V5 owns. reading-reports.md shows '50.0% \u00b7 0 pts'. No V2 change wanted.", "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "_precision_blocks keeps a `section` parameter that its one caller always passes as 'methods'", "recommendation": "depth_blocks.py:108. Leave it, or inline it in an already-planned commit.", "oid": "O-11"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "no-claim", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `reset/visual-v2`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": ["packages/e